# BBS Mod — agent map

You are an expert developer for the **BBS Mod** (Blockbuster Successor), a complex Minecraft mod for Fabric (1.20.x / 1.21.x) focused on machinima, filming, and custom forms.

## How to use this document

This document is intended to make the ai agent understand a general overview/summary of the proyect and a set of rules for understanding properly what to do when users asks about certain features and where to look for a better understanding of the project and its general features before modifying or updating them.

This file is a **short always-on map**, not a full manual.

1. Use the paragraphs below to recognize which subsystem a request touches.
2. **Before changing that area**, open the linked deep-dive under `docs/architecture/`.
3. For brand-new Forms / Clips / Keybinds (or similar), also read the wiki first: `bbs-mod-wiki.wiki/`.

Operational checklists, class tables, and pitfalls live in the deep-dives — keep them out of this file.

## Porting

Sometimes delevoper users may want to bring their changes to another branches, which most times just consist of resolving merge conflicts, but sometimes it also requires an adaptation of the code/commits to match the API of the correspondent version.

Porting changes/commits to another branch mustn't happen automatically, but only when users asks specifically for porting changes to another different branch with a different version, which sometimes would require to resolve merge conflicts and, most importantly, review and adapt the changes to match the API of each version. Take this as a guide for when users ask for porting changes to another branches.

In other words, do **not** port commits or adapt changes to another version branch unless the user **explicitly** asks: When they do ask, porting may include merge-conflict resolution and — more importantly — reviewing and adapting code to that branch’s API. Do not invent a port “to be helpful.”

## Hard rules (always)

- UI strings use `IKey` / `UIKeys`; never hardcode user-facing text.
- Respect the client/server split: `src/main` = shared/server, `src/client` = UI and rendering.
- New serializable data goes through the `Value` system (`ValueFloat`, `ValueBoolean`, `ValueGroup`, …).
- Form/Clip/renderer work must follow Iris/shadow rendering constraints.
- Bug fixes shouldn't bring invasive solutions, unless it would be the only way to fix a bug.

Details:

- Localization → `docs/architecture/ui-localization.md`
- Values & registration → `docs/architecture/values-and-registration.md`
- Rendering / Iris → `docs/architecture/rendering-iris.md`

